   "paragraph": "Buying shares gives a company an ownership stake in another business. Taiwan chipmaker TSMC’s board authorised two potential investments on November 10, with up to US$500 million for Anthropic common stock at its proposed public offering price and up to US$500 million for OpenAI preferred stock, shares with different rights from common shares. Think of approving a budget before making a purchase. The US$1 billion combined ceiling says how much TSMC can spend, while the amount it has actually invested remains unknown. Anthropic began presenting its proposed stock offering to investors that day, and its public listing was still pending.",
