   "paragraph": "When someone asks an AI model a question, computers have to run the trained model to produce the answer. That work is called inference. Think of a shop serving customers from a kitchen that another business equips and runs. Under an initial multiyear arrangement announced on November 10, Rackspace expects to operate dedicated Nvidia GB300 NVL72 systems for Together AI to handle those requests. Rackspace plans to supply the networking, electricity and cooling that keep the computers connected and running. Deployment is planned for 2027 and depends on conditions being met, so when the systems will actually begin serving requests remains uncertain.",
